{"id": "strategyqa_grounded/test/155", "source": "strategyqa_grounded", "primitive": "noul", "split": "test", "state": "{\"facts\": \"Door to door advertising involves someone going to several homes in a residential area to make sales and leave informational packets. During the COVID-19 pandemic, the CDC recommends that people limit their travel to essential needs only. During the COVID-19 pandemic, citizens are advised to stay home and to limit their interaction with others. During the COVID-19 pandemic, people are encouraged to remain six feet away from each other at all times. The more people that someone interacts with, the higher the likelihood of them becoming a vector for the COVID-19 virus.\", \"question\": \"During the pandemic, is door to door advertising considered inconsiderate?\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"noul\", \"instructions\": \"Given `facts`, is the answer to `question` yes?\"}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"ChilleD/StrategyQA\", \"license\": \"mit\", \"domain\": \"knowledge\", \"task_family\": \"grounded-yes-no\", \"qid\": \"8b41a17e65ef7f6e22b5\", \"term\": \"Advertising\"}"}
